# No Type Any - Use Specific Types (BLOCKING)

RULE: Use specific types (TypedDict, Pydantic, Protocol, dict[str, X]). Never use Any. Check dependency source code to determine actual type.
WHY: Any defeats type checking — no autocomplete, no refactoring safety, runtime errors instead of compile-time.
CODEX: 06-coding-standards/README.md#type-hints

DO:
  def process(data: dict[str, str]) -> str: return data.get("key", "")
  class Config(TypedDict): max_workers: int; venues: list[str]

NEVER:
  def process(data: Any) -> Any:
  config: dict[str, Any] = load_config()  # when you know the structure
